      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this fantastic three-bedroom semi detached property to the Dublin 10 property market. Ideally situated on the quiet, mature, and highly sought-after Ramillies Road,. A massive added advantage for prospective buyers is that this property qualifies for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant. This presents a phenomenal opportunity for first-time buyers, savvy renovators, or investors looking to add serious value in a vibrant, established residential setting.\nThe location is second to none. Ramillies Road sits within easy reach of Ballyfermot Village, offering a wealth of local amenities virtually on your doorstep, including reputable primary and secondary schools, local shops, supermarkets, cafes, and sports facilities. The idyllic grounds of Markievicz Park are just a short stroll away. Commuters will benefit from exceptional transport connections; frequent bus corridors provide swift, direct access into Dublin City Centre, while the Luas Red Line, Park West Train Station, and the M50/N7 motorways are all easily accessible by car.\nInternal living accommodation of c. 95 sqm is laid out over two floors and filled with natural light. Downstairs comprises a welcoming entrance hallway leading into a spacious front parlor/living room and an open plan kitchen and dining space. Upstairs features three generous bedrooms alongside a main family bathroom suite. In need of a touch of TLC throughout, this property offers a fantastic blank canvas for prospective buyers to modernize and put their own personal stamp on a classic home. Being a semi detached home, the property benefits from side entrance access to a private, low-maintenance rear garden, ideal for outdoor relaxation or family entertaining.\nViewing is highly advised. Call RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today for further information or to arrange a viewing!\nAdditional Features;\n•c. 95 sqm\n•BER F\n•3 BED / 1 BATH\n•Incredible potential to modernize & capitalize on grant funding\n•Bright and spacious interior layout\n•Three generous bedrooms upstairs\n•Private, low-maintenance rear garden space\n•Quiet, mature, and highly desirable residential road\n•Short walking distance to Ballyfermot Village & Markievicz Park\n•Excellent public transport routes into Dublin City Centre\n•Easy access to Luas Red Line, M50 motorway & N7\n•Ideal for First-Time Buyers, Renovators, and Investors alike\nDirections\nFrom the Red Cow Roundabout, take the exit onto the Naas Road heading inbound toward Dublin City Centre. Turn left at the major junction onto Kylemore Road and proceed straight through the traffic lights toward Ballyfermot. Turn left onto Ballyfermot Road, then take a right turn onto Blackditch Road. Continue straight and turn left onto Ramillies Road. Follow the road along, and No. 57 will be located on your right-hand side, clearly identified by our Ray Cooke Auctioneers 'For Sale' sign.\n"
      },
